n\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle II does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles I and III covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436043 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436043 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86864" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436043 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436043 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/bb/bbc1bc7b3bb910ffbd13571283bbfa305404d13eb2cb3b5ab423a1c02e46ab86.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. ${∬}_{R}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,2]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,2]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436043 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7e910b3-a1a9-5ea8-8009-6cb31a154137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436043 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436044 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436044 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "151f4abe-23c3-58b1-8e53-69be8020bff5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436044 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436045 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436045 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "36b5039d-7687-54cd-9c71-0a7c40931970" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436045 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186348410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436046 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8d37cf97-1bdd-5ae3-a97c-0f1ffc62d78b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436046 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436043 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
